{ns}
{define: CaddG base-fret 1 frets x 3 2 0 1 3} 
{define: Dsus4 base-fret 1 frets x x 0 2 3 3} 
{define: Gadd base-fret 1 frets 3 2 0 0 3 3} 
{t: FOREVER YOUNG – Nitty Gritty Dirt Band }
{st: (Dylan) }
{artist: Nitty Gritty Dirt Band }
{composer: Bob Dylan }


https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=R5AizC8OU_c  (Capo 0) (MC 1/5)

TIP:  The intro can be played with just the major chords but the adds bring in the sparkly treble.

TIP:  If transposing, play the root of the transposed (CaddG) and (Gadd) and add the 5th note as needed. 

TIP:  The outro instrumental can be a bit tricky.  The chords without a dash between them, e.g. (G) (D) (G) are full measures and with the dash, e.g. (G) - (D) - (G) are half measures.


